public import Mathlib.Tactic.FinCases

/-!
# Multiplication certificate for rows 96 through 127

This is one part of the multiplication check for the explicit 128-element
permutation model. Separate compilation bounds the kernel's reduction cache;
`Certificates.row_product` combines the four parts. Every equation is checked
by kernel reduction of the tables generated by `source/generate.py`.

Source of the exclusion problem: Huppert--Blackburn III, XII.1.18(b), p.314.
-/

namespace Theory.GroupTheory.HeldM22A10.ThirdExclusion.Tables
set_option maxRecDepth 100000

set_option maxHeartbeats 1000000 in
private theorem product_row_96 : ∀ j x, row (product 96 j) x = row 96 (row j x) := by
  decide +kernel

